    "description": "Dereferencing is the action to access a value, which is referenced with a pointer. Since PHP has no pointer, dereferencing applies to accessing an element in an array or an object. \n\nDereferencing is also possible to function and methods calls: when a function returns an array or an object, it is possible to immediately access one of the element by using the array or method syntax.",
    "code": "<?php\n\n$array = ['a', 'b', 'c'];\n\necho $array['b'];\n\nfunction trumpet() {\n    return ['x', 'y', 'z'];\n}\n\n// Function Array Dereferencing\ntrumpet()[2]; // display z\n\n?>",
